  "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the elliptic cone and the plane $z=-3,$ we substitute $z=-3$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & =(-3+7)^{2} \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{(2)^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with a semi-major axis of length $a=2.$ Therefore, the major axis has length $2a=4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
